71: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
72:     """
73:     Move the left-edge fragment into its same-colored anchor fragment to complete a solid rectangle.
74: 
75:     Input structure
76:     - The grid has a dominant background color.
77:     - Exactly one foreground color is split into two 4-connected objects: one
78:       touches the left edge, and the other is an anchor away from the left edge.
79:     - The translated left-edge object and the anchor can form one filled rectangle.
80:     Rule
81:     - Find the unique split color whose left-edge object can be translated onto
82:       background cells beside the other same-colored object so their union is a
83:       solid axis-aligned rectangle.
84:     - Clear the left-edge object's original cells to the background.
85:     - Paint that object at the unique completing offset, preserving all other cells.
86:     Key insight
87:     - The active color is identified by object structure and rectangle completion,
88:       not by a fixed color id; the same-colored anchor object stays in place.
