7: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
8:     """
9:     Select the color of the largest contiguous non-background object and return it as a solid 3x3 block.
10: 
11:     Input structure:
12:     - The background is the dominant color.
13:     - Some foreground colors are scattered clutter split into many 4-connected components.
14:     - The meaningful foreground objects are colors whose pixels form exactly one 4-connected object.
15: 
16:     Rule:
17:     - For each non-background color, count its 4-connected monochrome components.
18:     - Among the colors with exactly one such object, choose the unique largest by pixel area.
19:     - Fill the fixed 3x3 output grid with that object's color.
20: 
21:     Key insight:
22:     - Clutter colors may have high total frequency, but they are fragmented; the answer is the biggest whole object color.
23:     """
